WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.648 --> 00:00:08.017
Trying to raise family in Alaska.

00:00:08.384 --> 00:00:10.987
Not exactly safe.
You just need to keep your eye out.

00:00:10.987 --> 00:00:13.056
That's why I start packing a little bit
bigger gun.

00:00:14.057 --> 00:00:16.459
We really came out here
just to follow our dream

00:00:16.459 --> 00:00:19.929
of living the subsistence life.

00:00:19.929 --> 00:00:21.431
If I was a brand new a rookie out

00:00:21.431 --> 00:00:24.133
here, I'd be scared to death.

00:00:25.034 --> 00:00:28.071
It is great living,
but it's easy dying out here as well.

00:00:28.538 --> 00:00:31.875
All of our hands
have a little blood on them,

00:00:32.609 --> 00:00:35.511
and if the predators
aren't out to get you, the weather is.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.322
Okay, you're gonna want to watch out.

00:00:49.259 --> 00:00:52.528
Are we going to build, like,
a little railing on the porch or anything?

00:00:52.528 --> 00:00:53.463
I don't know about a railing,

00:00:53.463 --> 00:00:56.699
but I was thinking,
so the roof will hang over right here.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.701
We'll have two posts coming up.

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:00.370
I like your idea.

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:03.206
This is very much bigger
than your average dog house.

00:01:06.175 --> 00:01:06.576
I want

00:01:06.576 --> 00:01:09.479
the three bigger dogs to all be able
to fit in there together.

00:01:09.646 --> 00:01:10.980
Olivez, come here...and

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:14.851
provide a space to get out of the rain,
out of the snow and out of the elements.

00:01:14.851 --> 00:01:15.752
Should love on Olivez.

00:01:15.752 --> 00:01:19.255
She's having a pretty rough time
getting around with all those puppies

00:01:19.255 --> 00:01:20.256
sitting on her tummy.

00:01:20.256 --> 00:01:22.392
How many puppies do
you think she's going to have?

00:01:22.392 --> 00:01:23.426
Seven or five.

00:01:23.426 --> 00:01:26.462
Seven, or five?

00:01:26.462 --> 00:01:29.632
She's planning on a two hundred
thousand hundred.

00:01:30.366 --> 00:01:32.402
Yeah. Yup. Too many.

00:01:32.402 --> 00:01:36.572
All right Olivez, we got to get to work
because we're going to take the trees

00:01:36.572 --> 00:01:37.240
that we got.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.742
We're going to cut them the length
and strip the bark off of them,

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:41.611
with some draw knives.

00:01:41.611 --> 00:01:44.414
That doesn't have to be perfect,
we just want enough off

00:01:44.414 --> 00:01:47.717
to where the moisture
will not stay in there and rot.

00:01:49.552 --> 00:01:50.353
You want some help.

00:01:50.353 --> 00:01:52.422
Yes and no.

00:01:52.422 --> 00:01:53.356
Yes and no?

00:01:53.356 --> 00:01:53.923
Yeah. Watch.

00:01:56.392 --> 00:01:57.694
Do you want to try?

00:01:57.694 --> 00:01:59.429
You can always get that
with a [inaudible].

00:01:59.429 --> 00:02:03.132
Will you turn my [inaudible] like this?

00:02:03.132 --> 00:02:06.002
Can you skoot the, can you skoot the log
that way so I can roll it?

00:02:09.038 --> 00:02:10.673
You can always hand her the chainsaw.

00:02:12.542 --> 00:02:14.510
Not this time around.

00:02:16.346 --> 00:02:18.014
To gain knowledge

00:02:18.014 --> 00:02:22.919
as a child, of how to do adult things
that is so valuable.

00:02:22.919 --> 00:02:26.089
Like all of these skills,
these are things that typically aren't

00:02:26.089 --> 00:02:27.390
really taught in school.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.525
That parts kind of hard
because its got knots in it.

00:02:29.792 --> 00:02:32.729
Here I'll turn it
and maybe try, like this part.

00:02:32.762 --> 00:02:33.463
Okay?

00:02:33.696 --> 00:02:36.933
I think I got all the easy stuff
and you got all the hard stuff to do.

00:02:36.933 --> 00:02:39.936
You're doing pretty good. I got
easy stuff. Oh, you did?

00:02:39.936 --> 00:02:40.703
Oh Okay.

00:02:42.438 --> 00:02:44.907
Lily is checking it out.

00:02:49.679 --> 00:02:50.646
See where this one is?

00:02:50.646 --> 00:02:51.180
Right there.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.950
I went in from the side at an angle.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:56.519
You see how solid that is?
That ain't moving. Wow.

00:02:56.686 --> 00:02:59.322
This is going to be fantastic.

00:03:00.523 --> 00:03:01.791
I like being away from people.

00:03:01.791 --> 00:03:03.893
Like being away from modern technology.

00:03:03.893 --> 00:03:07.764
I like to disconnect, create my own world.

00:03:07.764 --> 00:03:10.867
Now live like people lived in the past.

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:14.871
All right.

00:03:14.871 --> 00:03:17.707
Coming up to the snare line.

00:03:17.707 --> 00:03:19.175
The first one right there.

00:03:19.175 --> 00:03:21.778
Easy enough. It's empty.

00:03:22.311 --> 00:03:24.380
My paycheck out here
doesn't come in the form of money.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:27.550
It comes in the form of meat
and I need to find more meat.

00:03:29.986 --> 00:03:33.122
I need to center it a little bit more.

00:03:33.122 --> 00:03:33.723
All right.

00:03:33.823 --> 00:03:35.458
Keep on checking.

00:03:35.858 --> 00:03:38.861
You know, it's interesting, because I made
these paths with my snowshoes

00:03:39.462 --> 00:03:42.331
and now I don't need snowshoes anymore
because it packs down

00:03:42.331 --> 00:03:43.633
and it freezes overnight.

00:03:43.633 --> 00:03:45.468
And the solution here is kind of
do the same thing.

00:03:45.468 --> 00:03:47.370
They just go in the same exact place.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.772
So they're making little highways
I'm making little highways.

00:03:49.906 --> 00:03:52.041
Everything I do out here,
I'm learning from the animals.

00:03:53.576 --> 00:03:55.778
See what's happening here?

00:03:56.079 --> 00:03:58.247
Nothing. Trap looks good.

00:03:58.247 --> 00:04:01.851
No new tracks at all around it.

00:04:03.286 --> 00:04:04.654
Keep on checking.

